  "name": "Extent and Conditions of Ice for Danish Harbors in the North Pole Area (1951)",
  "description": "Publication Title: Isforholdene i de Arktiske Have 1951 = The state of the ice in the Arctic Seas 1951 / [prepared by Helge Thomsen and M.V.L. Lorck]. Call number: QC994.8.I8 1951 archive - available at the National Climatic Data Center Library, Asheville, North Carolina, U.S.A. Appendix to the Nautical-meteorological annual 1951. Includes narrative information and monthly charts of the North Pole area showing unbroken polar ice, land floe, great ice fields, tight ice, young ice, and ice bergs.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: This publication is in the National Climatic Data Center's Foreign Data Library, and is one of many books, atlases, maps, charts and other printed materials received by the NCDC from many nations over the years.",
